{
  "title": "29: al-Ankaboot العنكبوت",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓمّٓ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nALIF LAAAM MEEM.\nAlif, Lam, Meem.\nاَحَسِبَ النَّاسُ اَنْ يُّتْرَكُوْۤا اَنْ يَّقُوْلُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا وَهُمْ لَا يُفْتَنُوْنَ‏(2)\nA-HASEBAN NAASO ANY YUTRAKOO ANY YAQOOLOO AAMAANNAA WA HUM LAA YUFTANOON.\nDo the people suppose that they will be let off because they say, ‘We have faith,’ and they will not be tested?\nوَلَقَدْ فَتَنَّا الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ فَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ صَدَقُوْا وَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(3)\nWA LAQAD FATANNAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FA-LA-YA’LAMANNAL LAAHUL LAZEENA SADAQOO WA LA-YA’LAMANNAL KAAZEBEEN.\nCertainly We tested those who were before them. So Allah shall surely ascertain those who are truthful, and He shall surely ascertain the liars.\nاَمْ حَسِبَ الَّذِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ اَنْ يَّسْبِقُوْنَا‌ ؕ سَآءَ مَا يَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(4)\nAM HASEBAL LAZEENA YA’MALOONAS SAYYEAATE ANY YASBEQOONAA, SAAA-A MAA YAHKOMOON.\nDo those who commit misdeeds suppose that they can outmaneuver Us? Evil is the judgement that they make.\nمَنْ كَانَ يَرْجُوْا لِقَآءَ اللّٰهِ فَاِنَّ اَجَلَ اللّٰهِ لَاٰتٍ‌ؕ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(5)\nMAN KAANA YARJOO LE-QAAA-AL LAAHE FA-INNA AJALAL LAAHE LA-AAT, WA HOWAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nWhoever expects to encounter Allah [should know that] Allah’s [appointed] time will indeed come, and He is the All-hearing, the All-knowing.\nوَمَنْ جَاهَدَ فَاِنَّمَا يُجَاهِدُ لِنَفْسِهٖؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَغَنِىٌّ عَنِ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(6)\nWA MAN JAAHADA FA-INNAMAA YOJAAHEDO LE-NAFSEH, INNAL LAAHA LA-GHANIYYUN A’NIL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhoever strives, strives only for his own sake. Indeed Allah has no need of the creatures.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَنُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ وَلَنَجْزِيَنَّهُمْ اَحْسَنَ الَّذِىْ كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(7)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LA-NOKAFFERANNA A’NHUM SAYYEAATEHIM WA LANAJZEYANNAHUM AHSANAL LAZEE KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAs for those who have faith and do righteous deeds, We will absolve them of their misdeeds and We will surely reward them by the best of what they used to do.\nوَوَصَّيْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ بِوَالِدَيْهِ حُسْنًا‌ ؕ وَاِنْ جَاهَدٰكَ لِتُشْرِكَ بِىْ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ فَلَا تُطِعْهُمَا ؕ اِلَىَّ مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَاُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(8)\nWA WASSAYNAL INSAANA BE-WAALEDAYHE HUSNAA, WA IN JAAHADAAKA LE-TUSHREKA BEE MAA LAYSA LAKA BEHI I’LMUN FALAA TO-TE’HOMAA, ELAYYA MARJE-O’KUM FA-ONABBE-OKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nWe have enjoined man to be good to his parents. But if they urge you to ascribe to Me as partner that of which you have no knowledge, then do not obey them. To Me will be your return, whereat I will inform you concerning what you used to do.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَنُدْخِلَنَّهُمْ فِى الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(9)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LANUDKHELANNAHUM FIS SAALEHEEN.\nThose who have faith and do righteous deeds, We will surely admit them among the righteous.\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَّقُوْلُ اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ فَاِذَاۤ اُوْذِىَ فِى اللّٰهِ جَعَلَ فِتْنَةَ النَّاسِ كَعَذَابِ اللّٰهِؕ وَلَئِنْ جَآءَ نَصْرٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اِنَّا كُنَّا مَعَكُمْ‌ؕ اَوَلَيْسَ اللّٰهُ بِاَعْلَمَ بِمَا فِىْ صُدُوْرِ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(10)\nWA MENAN NAASE MANY YAQOOLO AAMANNAA BIL LAAHE FA-EZAA OOZEYA FIL LAAHE JA-A’LA FITNATAN NAASE KA-A’ZAABIL LAAH, WA LAIN JAAA-A NASRUM MIR RABBEKA LA-YAQOOLUNNA INNAA KUNNAA MA-A’KUM, AWA LAYSAL LAAHO BE-A’ALAMA BEMAA FEE SODOORIL A’ALAMEEN.\nAmong the people there are those who say, ‘We have faith in Allah,’ but if such a one is tormented in Allah’s cause, he takes persecution by the people for Allah’s punishment. Yet if there comes any help from your Lord, they will say, ‘We were indeed with you.’ Does not Allah know best what is in the breasts of the creatures?\nوَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ‏(11)\nWA LA-YA’LAMANAL LAAHUL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA LA-YA’LAMANNAL MONAAFEQEEN.\nAllah shall surely ascertain those who have faith, and He shall surely ascertain the hypocrites.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّبِعُوْا سَبِيْلَنَا وَلْنَحْمِلْ خَطٰيٰكُمْ ؕ وَمَا هُمْ بِحٰمِلِيْنَ مِنْ خَطٰيٰهُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LIL-LAZEENA AAMANUT TABE-O’O SABEELANAA WAL NAHMIL KHATAAYAAKUM, WA MAA HUM BE-HAAMELEENA MIN KHATAAYAAHUM MIN SHAY, INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nThe faithless say to the faithful, ‘Follow our way and we will bear [responsibility for] your iniquities.’ They will not bear anything of their iniquities. They are indeed liars.\nوَلَيَحْمِلُنَّ اَ ثْقَالَهُمْ وَاَ ثْقَالًا مَّعَ اَثْقَالِهِمْ‌ وَلَيُسْئَلُنَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ عَمَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWA LAYAHMELUNNA ASQAALAHUM WA ASQAALAM MA-A’ ASQAALEHIM, WA LA-YUS-ALUNNA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE A’MMAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nBut they will carry their own burdens and other burdens along with their own burdens, and they will surely be questioned on the Day of Resurrection concerning that which they used to fabricate.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ فَلَبِثَ فِيْهِمْ اَ لْفَ سَنَةٍ اِلَّا خَمْسِيْنَ عَامًا ؕ فَاَخَذَهُمُ الطُّوْفَانُ وَهُمْ ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA NOOHAN ELAA QAWMEHI FALABESA FEEHIM ALFA SANATIN ILLAA KHAMSEENA A’AMAA, FA-AKHAZNAAHOMUT TOOFAANO WA HUM ZAALEMOON.\nCertainly We sent Noah to his people, and he remained with them for a thousand-less-fifty years. Then the flood overtook them while they were wrongdoers.\nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَاَصْحٰبَ السَّفِيْنَةِ وَجَعَلْنٰهَاۤ اٰيَةً لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(15)\nFA-ANJAYNAAHO WA ASHAABAS SAFEENATE WA JA-A’LNAAHAA AAYATAL LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nThen We delivered him and those who were in the Ark, and made it a sign for all the nations.\nوَاِبْرٰهِيْمَ اِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَاتَّقُوْهُ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(16)\nWA IBRAAHEEMA IZ QAALA LE-QAWMEHI’ BODUL LAAHA WAT-TAQOOH, ZAALEKUM KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nAnd Abraham, when he said to his people, ‘Worship Allah and be wary of Him. That is better for you, should you know.\nاِنَّمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَوْثَانًا وَّتَخْلُقُوْنَ اِفْكًا‌ ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ لَكُمْ رِزْقًا فَابْتَغُوْا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الرِّزْقَ وَاعْبُدُوْهُ وَاشْكُرُوْا لَهٗ ؕ اِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(17)\nINNAMAA TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE AWSAANANW WA TAKHLOQOONA IFKAA, INNAL LAZEENA TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAA YAMLEKOONA LAKUM RIZQAN FAB-TAGHOO I’NDAL LAAHIR RIZQA WA’BODOOHO WASH KOROO LAH, ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nWhat you worship instead of Allah are mere idols, and you invent a lie. Indeed those whom you worship besides Allah have no control over your provision. So seek all [your] provision from Allah, and worship Him and thank Him, and to Him you shall be brought back.’\nوَاِنْ تُكَذِّبُوْا فَقَدْ كَذَّبَ اُمَمٌ مِّنْ قَبْلِكُمْ‌ؕ وَمَا عَلَى الرَّسُوْلِ اِلَّا الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(18)\nWA IN TOKAZZEBOO FAQAD KAZZABA OMAMUM MIN QABLEKUM, WA MAA A’LAR RASOOLE ILLAL BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nIf you impugn [the Apostle’s teaching], then [other] nations have impugned [likewise] before you, and the Apostle’s duty is only to communicate in clear terms.\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا كَيْفَ يُبْدِئُ اللّٰهُ الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيْدُهٗ ؕ اِنَّ ذٰ لِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ يَسِيْرٌ‏(19)\nAWA LAM YARAW KAYFA YUBDEUL LAAHUL KHALQA SUMMA YO-E’EDOH, INNA ZAALEKA A’LAL LAAHE YASEER.\nHave they not regarded how Allah originates the creation? Then He will bring it back. That is indeed easy for Allah.\nقُلْ سِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَانْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ بَدَاَ الْخَلْقَ‌ ثُمَّ اللّٰهُ يُنْشِئُ النَّشْاَةَ الْاٰخِرَةَ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‌ۚ‏(20)\nQUL SEEROO FIL ARZE FAN-ZOROO KAYFA BA-DA-AL KHALQA SUMMAL LAAHO YUNSHE-UN NASH-ATAL AAKHERAH, INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAYIN QADEER.\nSay, ‘Travel over the land and observe how He has originated the creation.’ Then Allah will bring about the genesis of the Hereafter. Indeed Allah has power over all things.\nيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَرْحَمُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ‌ۚ وَاِلَيْهِ تُقْلَبُوْنَ‏(21)\nYO-A’ZZEBO MANY YASHAAA-O WA YARHAMO MANY YASHAAA, WA ELAYHE TUQLABOON.\nHe will punish whomever He wishes and have mercy on whomever He wishes, and to Him you will be returned.\nوَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فِى السَّمَآءِ‌ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(22)\nWA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEENA FIL ARZE WA LAA FIS SAMAAA, WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MINW WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nYou cannot frustrate Him on the earth or in the sky, nor do you have besides Allah any guardian or helper.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَلِقَآئِهٖۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ يَئِسُوْا مِنْ رَّحْمَتِىْ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(23)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WA LEQAAA-EHI OOLAAA-EKA YA-ESOO MIR RAHMATEE WA OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nThose who deny the signs of Allah and the encounter with Him—they have despaired of My mercy, and for such there is a painful punishment.\nفَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوا اقْتُلُوْهُ اَوْ حَرِّقُوْهُ فَاَنْجٰٮهُ اللّٰهُ مِنَ النَّارِ ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(24)\nFAMAA KAANA JAWAABA QAWMEHI ILLAAA AN QAALUQ TOLOOHO AW HARREQOOHO FA-ANJAAHUL LAAHO MENAN NAAR, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nBut the only answer of his people was that they said, ‘Kill him, or burn him.’ Then Allah delivered him from the fire. There are indeed signs in that for a people who have faith.\nوَقَالَ اِنَّمَا اتَّخَذْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَوْثَانًا ۙ مَّوَدَّةَ بَيْنِكُمْ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ‌ۚ ثُمَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ يَكْفُرُ بَعْضُكُمْ بِبَعْضٍ وَّيَلْعَنُ بَعْضُكُمْ بَعْضًا  وَّمَاْوٰٮكُمُ النَّارُ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ نّٰصِرِيْنَ ۙ‏(25)\nWA QAALA INNAMAT TAKHAZTUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE AWSAANAM, MAWADDATA BAYNAKUM FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA, SUMMA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE YAKFORO BA’ZOHUM BE-BA’ZINW WA YAL-A’NO BA’ZOKUM BA’ZANW, WA MAAWAAKUMUN NAARO WA MAA LAKUM MIN NAASEREEN.\nHe said, ‘You have taken idols [for worship] besides Allah for the sake of [mutual] affection amongst yourselves in the life of the world. Then on the Day of Resurrection you will disown one another and curse one another, and the Fire will be your abode, and you will not have any helpers.’\nفَاٰمَنَ لَهٗ لُوْطٌ‌ۘ وَقَالَ اِنِّىْ مُهَاجِرٌ اِلٰى رَبِّىْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(26)\nFA-AAMANA LAHU LOOT, WA QAALA INNEE MOHAAJERUN ELAA RABBEE, INNAHU HOWAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nThereupon Lot believed in him, and he said, ‘Indeed I am migrating toward my Lord. Indeed He is the All-mighty, the All-wise.’\nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهٗۤ اِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ وَجَعَلْنَا فِىْ ذُرِّيَّتِهِ النُّبُوَّةَ وَالْكِتٰبَ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ اَجْرَهٗ فِى الدُّنْيَا ‌ۚ وَاِنَّهٗ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ لَمِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(27)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHU ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA WA JA-A’LNAA FEE ZURRIYYATEHIN NOBUWWATA WAL KETAABA WA AATAYNAAHO AJRAHU FID DUNYAA, WA INNAHU FIL AAKHERATE LAMENAS SAALEHEEN.\nAnd We gave him Isaac and Jacob, and We ordained among his descendants prophethood and the Book, and We gave him his reward in this world, and in the Hereafter he will indeed be among the Righteous.\nوَلُوْطًا اِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اِنَّكُمْ لَتَاْتُوْنَ الْفَاحِشَةَ مَا سَبَقَكُمْ بِهَا مِنْ اَحَدٍ مِّنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(28)\nWA LOOTAN IZ QAALA LEQAWMEHI INNAKUM LA-TAATOONAL FAAHESHAH, MAA SABAQAKUM BEHAA MIN AHADIM MENAL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd Lot, when he said to his people, ‘You indeed commit an indecency none in the world has ever committed before you!\nاَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَاْتُوْنَ الرِّجَالَ وَتَقْطَعُوْنَ السَّبِيْلَ ۙ وَتَاْ تُوْنَ فِىْ نَادِيْكُمُ الْمُنْكَرَ ‌ؕ فَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوا ائْتِنَا بِعَذَابِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(29)\nA-INNAKUM LA-TAA-TOONAR REJAALA WA TAQTA-O’ONAS SABEEL, WA TAA-TOONA FEE NAADEEKOMUL MUNKAR, FAMAA KAANA JAWAABA QAWMEHI ILLAA AN QAALOO E-ATENAA BE-A’ZAABIL LAAHE IN KUNTA MENAS SAADEQEEN.\nWhat! Do you come to men, and cut off the way, and commit outrages in your gatherings?’ But the only answer of his people was that they said, ‘Bring down us Allah’s punishment, if you are truthful.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ انْصُرْنِىْ عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(30)\nQAALA RABBIN SURNEE A’LAL QAWMIL MUFSEDEEN.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! Help me against this corruptive lot.’\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَتْ رُسُلُنَاۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ بِالْبُشْرٰىۙ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا مُهْلِكُوْۤا اَهْلِ هٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ ‌ۚ اِنَّ اَهْلَهَا كَانُوْا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(31)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-AT ROSOLONAA IBRAAHEEMA BIL-BUSHRAA, QAALOO INNAA MOHLEKOO AHLE HAAZEHIL QARYAH, INNA AHLAHAA KAANOO ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd when Our messengers came to Abraham with the good news, they said, ‘We are indeed going to destroy the people of this town. Its people are indeed wrongdoers.’\nقَالَ اِنَّ فِيْهَا لُوْطًا ‌ؕ قَالُوْا نَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ فِيْهَا‌ لَنُنَجِّيَنَّهٗ وَاَهْلَهٗۤ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَهٗ كَانَتْ مِنَ الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(32)\nQAALA INNA FEEHAA LOOTAA, QAALOO NAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAN FEEHAA, LA-NONAJJE-YANNAHU WA AHLAHU ILLAM RA-ATAH, KAANAT MENAL GHAABEREEN.\nHe said, ‘Lot is in it.’ They said, ‘We know better those who are in it. We will surely deliver him and his family, except his wife: she shall be one of those who remain behind.’\nوَلَمَّاۤ اَنْ جَآءَتْ رُسُلُنَا لُوْطًا سِىْٓءَ بِهِمْ وَضَاقَ بِهِمْ ذَرْعًا وَّقَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ وَلَا تَحْزَنْ‌ اِنَّا مُنَجُّوْكَ وَاَهْلَكَ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَكَ كَانَتْ مِنَ الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(33)\nWA LAMMAA AN JAAA-AT ROSOLONAA LOOTAN SEEE-A BEHIM WA ZAAQA BEHIM ZAR-A’NW WA QAALOO LAA TAKHAF WA LAA TAHZAN, INNAA MONAJJOOKA WA AHLAKA ILLAM RA-ATAKA KAANAT MENAL GHAABEREEN.\nAnd when Our messengers came to Lot, he was distressed on their account and in a predicament for their sake. But they said, ‘Do not be afraid, nor grieve! We shall deliver you and your family, except your wife: she will be one of those who remain behind.\nاِنَّا مُنْزِلُوْنَ عَلٰٓى اَهْلِ هٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ رِجْزًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْسُقُوْنَ‏(34)\nINNAA MUNZELOONA A’LAA AHLE HAAZEHIL QARYAHTE RIJZAM MENAS SAMAAA-E BEMAA KAANOO YAFSOQOON.\nWe are indeed going to bring down upon the people of this town a punishment from the sky because of the transgressions they used to commit.’\nوَلَقَد تَّرَكْنَا مِنْهَاۤ اٰيَةًۢ بَيِّنَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ‏(35)\nWA LAQAD TARAKNAA MINHAA AAYATAM BAYYENATIL LEQAWMINY YA’QELOON.\nCertainly We have left of it a manifest sign for people who exercise their reason.\nوَاِلٰى مَدْيَنَ اَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا ۙ فَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَ ارْجُوا الْيَوْمَ الْاٰخِرَ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(36)\nWA ELAA MADYANA AKHAAHUM SHO-A’YBAA, FAQAALA YAA QAWME’ BODUL LAAHA WAR JUL YAWMAL AAKHERA WA LAA TA’SAW FIL ARZE MUFSEDEEN.\nAnd to Midian We sent Shu‘ayb, their brother. He said, ‘O my people! Worship Allah, and expect [to encounter] the Last Day, and do not act wickedly on the earth causing corruption.’\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَ‏(37)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA-AKHAZATHOMUR RAJFATO FA-ASBAHOO FEE DAAREHIM JAASEMEEN.\nBut they impugned him, whereupon the earthquake seized them, and they lay lifeless prostrate in their homes.\nوَعَادًا وَّثَمُوْدَا۟ وَقَدْ تَّبَيَّنَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ مَّسٰكِنِهِمْ‌ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ السَّبِيْلِ وَكَانُوْا مُسْتَبْصِرِيْنَۙ‏(38)\nWA A’ADANW WA SAMOODAA WA QAT TABAYYANA LAKUM MIM MASAAKENEHIM, WA ZAYYANA LAHOMUSH SHAYTAANO A-A’MAALAHUM FA-SADDAHUM A’NIS SABEELE WA KAANOO MUSTABSEREEN.\nAnd ‘Ad and Thamud, [whose fate] is evident to you from their habitations. Satan made their deeds seem decorous to them, thus he barred them from the way [of Allah], though they used to be perceptive.\nوَقَارُوْنَ وَفِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامٰنَ‌ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ مُّوْسٰى بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا كَانُوْا سٰبِقِيْنَ ‌ ۖ ‌ ۚ‏(39)\nWA QAAROONA WA FIR-A’WNA WA HAAMAAN, WA LAQAD JAAA-AHUM MOOSAA BIL-BAYYENAATE FAS-TAKBAROO FIL ARZE WA MAA KAANOO SAABEQEEN.\nAnd Korah, Pharaoh, and Haman. Certainly, Moses brought them manifest proofs, but they acted arrogantly in the land; though they could not outmaneuver [Allah].\nفَكُلًّا اَخَذْنَا بِذَنْۢبِهٖ‌ ۚ فَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِ حَاصِبًا‌ ۚ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ اَخَذَتْهُ الصَّيْحَةُ‌ ۚ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ خَسَفْنَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ‌ ۚ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ اَغْرَقْنَا‌ ۚ وَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيَظْلِمَهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(40)\nFA-KULLAN AKHAZNAA BE-ZAMBEH, FAMINHUM MAN ARSALNAA A’LAYHE HAASEBAA, WA MINHUM MAN AKHAZATHUS SAYHAH, WA MINHUM MAN AGRAQNAA, WA MAA KAANAL LAAHO LE-YAZLEMAHUM WA LAAKIN KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nSo We seized each [of them] for his sin: among them were those upon whom We unleashed a rain of stones, and among them were those who were seized by the Cry, and among them were those whom We caused the earth to swallow, and among them were those whom We drowned. It was not Allah who wronged them, but it was they who used to wrong themselves.\nمَثَلُ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَوْلِيَآءَ كَمَثَلِ الْعَنْكَبُوْتِ ‌ۖۚ اِتَّخَذَتْ بَيْتًا ‌ؕ وَ اِنَّ اَوْهَنَ الْبُيُوْتِ لَبَيْتُ الْعَنْكَبُوْتِ‌ۘ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(41)\nMASALUL LAZEENAT TAKHAZOO MIN DOONIL LAAHE AWLE-YAAA-A KAMASALIL A’NKABOOT, ITTAKHAZAT BAYTAA, WA INNA AWHANAL BOYOOTE LA-BAYTUL A’NKABOOT, LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nThe parable of those who take guardians instead of Allah is that of the spider that takes a home, and indeed the frailest of homes is the home of a spider, had they known!\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ شَىْءٍ‌ؕ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(42)\nINNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI MIN SHAY, WA HOWAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nAllah indeed knows whatever thing they invoke besides Him, and He is the All-mighty, the All-wise.\nوَتِلْكَ الْاَمْثَالُ نَضْرِبُهَا لِلنَّاسِ‌ۚ وَمَا يَعْقِلُهَاۤ اِلَّا الْعٰلِمُوْنَ‏(43)\nWA TILKAL AMSAALO NAZREBOHAA LIN-NAAS, WA MAA YA’QELOHAA ILLAL A’ALEMOON.\nWe draw these parables for mankind; but no one grasps them except those who have knowledge.\nخَلَقَ اللّٰهُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(44)\nKHALAQAL LAAHUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQ, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYATAL LIL MOAMENEEN.\nAllah created the heavens and the earth with consummate wisdom. There is indeed a sign in that for the faithful.\nاُتْلُ مَاۤ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْكَ مِنَ الْكِتٰبِ وَاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ ‌ؕ اِنَّ الصَّلٰوةَ تَنْهٰى عَنِ الْفَحْشَآءِ وَالْمُنْكَرِ‌ؕ وَلَذِكْرُ اللّٰهِ اَكْبَرُ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَصْنَعُوْنَ‏(45)\nUTLO MAAA OOHEYA ELAYKA MENAL KETAABE WA AQEMIS SALAAH, INNAS SALAATA TANHAA A’NIL FAHSHAAA-E WAL MUNKAR, WA LAZIKRUL LAAHE AKBAR, WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO MAA YASNA-O’ON.\nRecite what has been revealed to you of the Book, and maintain the prayer. Indeed the prayer restrains from indecent and wrongful conduct, and the remembrance of Allah is surely greater. And Allah knows whatever [deeds] you do.\nوَلَا تُجَادِلُوْٓا اَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ اِلَّا بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُۖ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مِنْهُمْ‌ وَقُوْلُوْٓا اٰمَنَّا بِالَّذِىْۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْنَا وَاُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ وَاِلٰهُنَا وَاِلٰهُكُمْ وَاحِدٌ وَّنَحْنُ لَهٗ مُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(46)\nWA LAA TOJAADELOO AHLAL KETAABE ILLAA BIL-LATEE HEYA AHSAN, ILLAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO MINHUM WA QOOLOO AAMANNAA BIL-LAZEE UNZELA ELAYNAA WA UNZELA ELAYKUM WA ELAAHONAA WA ELAAHOKUM WAAHEDUNW WA NAHNO LAHU MUSLEMOON.\nDo not argue with the People of the Book except in a manner which is best, except such of them as are wrongdoers, and say, ‘We believe in what has been sent down to us and in what has been sent down to you; our God and your God is one [and the same], and to Him do we submit.’\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ‌ؕ فَالَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ‌ۚ وَمِنْ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ مَنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِهٖ ‌ؕ وَ مَا يَجْحَدُ بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اِلَّا الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(47)\nWA KAZAALEKA ANZALNAA ELAYKAL KETAAB, FAL-LAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA YOAMENOONA BEH, WA MIN HAA-OO-LAAA-E MANY YOAMENO BEH, WA MAA YAJHADO BE-AAYAATENAA ILLAL KAAFEROON.\nThus We have sent down the Book to you; those to whom We have given the Book believe in it, and of these there are some who believe in it, and none contests Our signs except the faithless.\nوَمَا كُنْتَ تَتْلُوْا مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ مِنْ كِتٰبٍ وَّلَا تَخُطُّهٗ بِيَمِيْنِكَ‌ اِذًا لَّارْتَابَ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA KUNTA TATLOO MIN QABLEHI MIN KETAABINW WA LAA TAKHUTTOHU BE-YAMEENEKA EZAL LARTAABAL MUBTELOON.\nYou did not use to recite any scripture before it, nor did you write it with your right hand, for then the impugners would have been skeptical.\nبَلْ هُوَ اٰيٰتٌۢ بَيِّنٰتٌ فِىْ صُدُوْرِ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ‌ؕ وَمَا يَجْحَدُ بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اِلَّا الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(49)\nBAL HOWA AAYAATUM BAYYENAATUN FEE SODOORIL LAZEENA OOTUL I’LM, WA MAA YAJHADO BE-AAYAATENAA ILLAZ ZAALEMOON.\nIndeed, it is [present as] manifest signs in the breasts of those who have been given knowledge, and none contests Our signs except wrongdoers.\nوَقَالُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ اٰيٰتٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ‌ؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَا الْاٰيٰتُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَاِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا۟ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(50)\nWA QAALOO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE AAYAATUM MIR RABBEH, QUL INNAMAL AAYAATO I’NDAL LAAH, WA INNAMAA ANAA NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nThey say, ‘Why has not some sign been sent down to him from his Lord?’ Say, ‘These signs are only from Allah, and I am only a manifest warner.’\nاَوَلَمْ يَكْفِهِمْ اَنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ يُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَرَحْمَةً وَّذِكْرٰى لِقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(51)\nAWA LAM YAKFEHIM ANNAA ANZALNAA A’LAYKAL KETAABA YUTLAA A’LAYHIM, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-RAHMATANW WA ZIKRAA LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nDoes it not suffice them that We have sent down to you the Book which is recited to them? There is indeed in that a mercy and admonition for a people who have faith.\nقُلْ كَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْ شَهِيْدًا ‌ۚ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِالْبَاطِلِ وَكَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ ۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(52)\nQUL KAFAA BIL LAAHE BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM SHAHEEDAA, YA’LAMO MAA FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO BIL-BAATELE WA KAFAROO BIL LAAHE, OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nSay, ‘Allah suffices as a witness between me and you: He knows whatever there is in the heavens and the earth. Those who put faith in falsehood and defy Allah—it is they who are the losers.’\nوَيَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَكَ بِالْعَذَابِ‌ؕ وَلَوْلَاۤ اَجَلٌ مُّسَمًّى لَّجَآءَهُمُ الْعَذَابُؕ وَلَيَاْتِيَنَّهُمْ بَغْتَةً وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(53)\nWA YASTA’JELOONAKA BIL A’ZAAB, WA LAW LAA AJALUM MOSAMMAAL LA-JAAA-AHOMUL A’ZAAB, WA LAYAATEYANNAHUM BAGHTATANW WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nThey ask you to hasten the punishment. Yet were it not for a specified time, the punishment would have surely overtaken them. Surely, it will overtake them suddenly while they are unaware.\nيَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَكَ بِالْعَذَابِؕ وَ اِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ لَمُحِيْطَةٌۢ بِالْكٰفِرِيْنَۙ‏(54)\nYASTA’JELOONAKA BIL-A’ZAAB, WA INNA JAHANNAMA LA-MOHEETATUM BIL-KAAFEREEN.\nThey ask you to hasten the punishment, and indeed hell will besiege the faithless\nيَوْمَ يَغْشٰٮهُمُ الْعَذَابُ مِنْ فَوْقِهِمْ وَمِنْ تَحْتِ اَرْجُلِهِمْ وَيَقُوْلُ ذُوْقُوْا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(55)\nYAWMA YAGHSHAA-HOMUL A’ZAABO MIN FAWQEHIM WA MIN TAHTE ARJOLEHIM WA YAQOOLO ZOOQOO MAA KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\non the day when the punishment envelopes them, from above them and from under their feet, and He will say, ‘Taste what you used to do!’\nيٰعِبَادِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّ اَرْضِىْ وَاسِعَةٌ فَاِيَّاىَ فَاعْبُدُوْنِ‏(56)\nYAA E’BAADEYAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNA ARZEE WAASE-A’TUN FA-IYYAA-YA FA’BODOON.\nO My servants who have faith! My earth is indeed vast. So worship [only] Me.\nكُلُّ نَفْسٍ ذَآئِقَةُ الْمَوْتِ ثُمَّ اِلَيْنَا تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(57)\nKULLO NAFSIN ZAAA-EQATUL MAWT, SUMMA ELAYNAA TURJA-O’ON.\nEvery soul shall taste death. Then you shall be brought back to Us.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوْا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُمْ مِّنَ الْجَنَّةِ غُرَفًا تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ‌ؕ نِعْمَ اَجْرُ الْعٰمِلِيْنَ‌ۖ‏(58)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LA-NOBAWWE-ANNAHUM MENAL JANNATE GHORAFAN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, NE’MA AJRUL A’AMELEENAL.\nThose who have faith and do righteous deeds, We will surely settle them in the lofty abodes of paradise, with streams running in them, to remain in them [forever]. How excellent is the reward of the workers!\nالَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوْا وَعَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُوْنَ‏(59)\nLAZEENA SABAROO WA A’LAA RABBEHIM YATAWAKKALOON.\n—Those who are patient and who put their trust in their Lord.\nوَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ دَآبَّةٍ لَّا تَحْمِلُ رِزْقَهَاۖ اللّٰهُ يَرْزُقُهَا وَاِيَّاكُمْ‌‌ۖ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(60)\nWA KA-AYYIM MIN DAAAB-BATIL LAA TAHMELO RIZQAHAA, ALLAAHO YARZOQOHAA WA IYYAAKUM, WA HOWAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nHow many an animal there is that does not carry its own provision. Allah provides them and you, and He is the All-hearing, the All-knowing.\nوَلَئِنْ سَاَلْتَهُمْ مَّنْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَسَخَّرَ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اللّٰهُ‌ۚ فَاَنّٰى يُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA LAIN SA-ALTAHUM MAN KHALAQAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA SAKHKHARASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA LAYAQOOLUNNAL LAAH, FA-ANNAA YOAFEKOON.\nIf you ask them, ‘Who created the heavens and the earth, and who has disposed the sun and the moon?’ They will surely say, ‘Allah.’ Then where do they stray?\nاَللّٰهُ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَقْدِرُ لَهٗ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(62)\nALLAAHO YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMANY YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI WA YAQDERO LAH, INNAL LAAHA BEKULLE SHAYIN A’LEEM.\nAllah expands the provision for whomever He wishes of His servants, and tightens it for him. Indeed Allah has knowledge of all things.\nوَلَئِنْ سَاَلْتَهُمْ مَّنْ نَّزَّلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَاَحْيَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَوْتِهَا لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اللّٰهُ‌ؕ قُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(63)\nWA LAIN SA-ALTAHUM AMN NAZZALA MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA-AHYAA BEHIL ARZA MIM BA’DE MAWTEHAA LAYAQOOLUNNAL LAAH, QOLIL HAMDO LILLAAH, BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’QELOON.\nAnd if you ask them, ‘Who sends down water from the sky, with which He revives the earth after its death?’ They will surely say, ‘Allah.’ Say, ‘All praise belongs to Allah!’ But most of them do not exercise their reason.\nوَمَا هٰذِهِ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَاۤ اِلَّا لَهْوٌ وَّلَعِبٌ‌ؕ وَاِنَّ الدَّارَ الْاٰخِرَةَ لَهِىَ الْحَيَوَانُ‌ۘ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(64)\nWA MAA HAAZEHIL HAYAATUD DUNYAA ILLAA LAHWUNW WA LA-E’B, WA INNAD DAARAL AAKHERATA LAHEYAL HAYAWAAN, LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nThe life of this world is nothing but diversion and play, but the abode of the Hereafter is indeed Life (itself), had they known!\nفَاِذَا رَكِبُوْا فِى الْفُلْكِ دَعَوُا اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ ۚ فَلَمَّا نَجّٰٮهُمْ اِلَى الْبَرِّ اِذَا هُمْ يُشْرِكُوْنَۙ‏(65)\nFA-EZAA RAKEBOO FIL FULKE DA-A’WUL LAAHA MUKHLESEENA LAHUD DEEN, FALAMMAA NAJJAAHUM ELAL BARRE EZAA HUM YUSHREKOONA.\nWhen they board the ship, they invoke Allah putting exclusive faith in Him, but when He delivers them to land, behold, they ascribe partners [to Him],\nلِيَكْفُرُوْا بِمَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْۙۚ وَلِيَتَمَتَّعُوْا‌فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(66)\nLE-YAKFOROO BEMAA AATAYNAAHUM, WA LE-YATAMATTA-O’O, FA-SAWFA YA’LAMOON.\nbeing ungrateful for what We have given them! Let them enjoy. Soon they will know!\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّا جَعَلْنَا حَرَمًا اٰمِنًا وَّيُتَخَطَّفُ النَّاسُ مِنْ حَوْلِهِمْ‌ ؕ اَفَبِالْبَاطِلِ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ وَبِنِعْمَةِ اللّٰهِ يَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(67)\nAWA LAM YARAW ANNAA JA-A’LNAA HARAMAN AAMENANW WA YOTAKHATTAFUN NAASO MIN HAWLEHIM, AFA-BIL-BAATELE YOAMENOONA WA BE-NE’MATIL LAAHE YAKFOROON.\nHave they not seen that We have appointed a safe sanctuary, while the people are despoiled all around them? Would they then believe in falsehood and be ungrateful toward the blessing of Allah?\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَوْ كَذَّبَ بِالْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهٗ‌ؕ اَلَيْسَ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ مَثْوًى لِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(68)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AW KAZZABA BIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAA-AH, A-LAYSA FEE JAHANNAMA MASWAL LIL-KAAFEREEN.\nWho is a greater wrongdoer than him who fabricates a lie against Allah, or denies the truth when it comes to him? Is not the [final] abode of the faithless in hell?\nوَالَّذِيْنَ جَاهَدُوْا فِيْنَا لَنَهْدِيَنَّهُمْ سُبُلَنَا ‌ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَمَعَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(69)\nWAL LAZEENA JAAHADOO FEENAA LA-NAHDEYANNAHUM SOBOLANAA, WA INNAL LAAHA LA-MA-A’L MOHSENEEN.\nAs for those who strive in Us, We shall surely guide them in Our ways, and Allah is indeed with the virtuous.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Ankaboot (The Spider)\nThe first 11 verses of this Surah are ‘Madani’ and the rest were revealed in Makkah. This Surah has a total of 69 verses. In the commentary of Burhan it is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites Surah al-Ankaboot on the 23rd night of the month of Ramazan, will enter Paradise without any questioning.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward for reciting this Surah can be compared to ten times the number of believing men and women plus ten times the number of hypocrites on Earth. Drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved brings one great joy and happiness in his life."
